Room for every word a command writes.

CmdBufWriter::reserve(n) makes room for n words; the words after it are
written without a check, and a user command buffer keeps no spare words at
its memory's end. dkCmdBufBindVtxBuffers reserved 5 words a buffer and wrote
6 (VertexArray::Start and VertexArrayLimit, each a header and an address), so
binding many buffers near the end of command memory wrote up to numBuffers-1
words past it, into memory that something else then overwrote before the GPU
read it: on the console, after minutes of play, GPU method errors at
VertexArrayLimit[14] (the 15th buffer's) with a float or another command's
header as its address (2359-0001). Blit2DEngine reserved 38 words where the
premultiplied modes with two block-linear images write 39.

diff --git a/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_vbo.cpp b/source/maxwell/gpu_3d_vbo.cpp
